		"meta": {
			"author": "",
			"category": "source",
			"deploymentTarget": {
				"branch": "",
				"name": "Wire",
				"version": {
					"major": 7,
					"minor": 27,
					"patch": 0
				}
			},
			"description": "Star Globe - glowing stars inside a container like a snow globe: they fall with gravity and lie on the wall or simmer on it. Nothing moves by itself: drive 'Physics Clock' from Arena (BPM Sync or Timeline; 1 unit = 1 beat feels natural). Stars reflect off the wall (angle in = angle out). Bounce = repulsion of the wall: 0 = stars rest and only follow the line when the container moves; above 0 every touch sends them off with at least that speed, so they simmer on the line. Scatter (deg) is added to the outgoing angle of a share of the stars set by Chaos (0 = none, 1 = all) - all in the same direction, so the stars swirl. Air Drag slows stars in flight. Jolt Strength moves the container along Jolt Dir - fast changes (envelope, FFT, sawtooth) give the impulse. Jitter makes the container tremble while the clock runs (0 = still). Shape morphs the container: 0 oval\/circle, 1 polygon (Corners), 2 heart, 3 trapezoid; values in between blend. Stars: Star Size = radius of the solid core (also the distance to the wall and to other stars), Glow Size = radius of the soft glow behind it; cores are always drawn on top of all glows, so Star Color and Glow Color never mix. Collision: Collide On lets stars push each other apart like the wall does; Collide Force = how hard (too high makes the pile boil). Collision runs in the ISF shader StarGlobeCollide.fs, which must stay at its path. Backdrop On\/Off: On = solid Backdrop Color behind everything, Off = transparent background.",
			"displayName": "Star Globe",
			"identifier": "411754f4-84ed-4d7a-873a-c9ea523f6660",
			"licenseName": "",
			"mail": "",
