					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "Physics per star (feedback): V += gravity x dt, drag; P += V x dt. Collision in container space (rotated, scaled by Width\/Height): oval = radius limit, polygon = edge normal of the sector, heart\/trapezoid = radius table (256 angles), push along the table normal. Wall distance = visible star radius. Reflect outward speed with (1 + Bounce). Container offset = Jolt Direction x Jolt Strength x 0.1 + Jitter (Perlin of the clock); container movement kicks stars touching the wall inward. Stars do not collide with each other."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 1000,
